{#- host_port is not cAdvisor's usual 8080: qBittorrent already has that on
   arrstack.

   Raw-cgroup mode, no container runtime API: cAdvisor reads the cgroup tree
   (cgroupns=host + /sys/fs/cgroup bound read-only) and reports every cgroup
   under raw_cgroup_prefixes. A Quadlet container is
   id="/system.slice/<unit>.service/libpod-payload-<id>"; Prometheus derives
   `name` (= container name = unit name) from that (pillar/prometheus.sls,
   metric_relabel_configs on the cadvisor job). No podman socket (root-
   equivalent), not privileged, own user namespace — checked on homepage
   2026-11-12 with v0.60.6. docker_only stays on: it only means "no other
   raw cgroups than the whitelisted ones"; the runtime factories just fail
   to register (log lines at start, harmless).

   mine: Salt Mine entry the prometheus formula reads its cadvisor targets
   from (mine.get('*', alias)) — only minions with this formula have it.
   interface: network.ip_addrs without it also returns podman0's address.

   podman: spec overrides for the container (keys: formulas/podman README). #}
{%- set defaults = {
    'image': 'ghcr.io/google/cadvisor',
    'tag': 'v0.60.6',
    'container_name': 'cadvisor',
    'host_port': 8088,
    'housekeeping_interval': '30s',
    'raw_cgroup_prefixes': ['/system.slice/'],
    'podman': {},
    'mine': {
        'alias': 'cadvisor',
        'interface': 'eth0',
        'conf': '/etc/salt/minion.d/mine-cadvisor.conf',
        'event_tag': 'homelab/mine/updated',
    },
} %}
{%- set cadvisor = salt['pillar.get']('cadvisor:lookup', default=defaults, merge=True) %}
